  nonce: 43d4  # 43d4
  message: "Dogfood finding (member F159.A2-b, split from F159.A2), reproduces on the frozen substrate. Mechanism: the websocket-linker's pattern-type->framework map (_PATTERN_TYPE_TO_FRAMEWORK) assigns a framework string from the matched pattern type alone, with no check against installed dependencies. The matched WS pattern resolves to fastapi regardless of what the repo actually depends on. Scope: 6 cross-language WS calls edges carry meta.server_framework=\"fastapi\" while FastAPI is not in any manifest; the repo's actual server framework is starlette (which also appears, 6 edges). Affects WS linker edges on any repo whose WS patterns resemble FastAPI's. Exposure/consequence: any consumer reading server_framework to learn which web framework serves a repo's WS endpoints concludes the repo runs FastAPI and may propose FastAPI-specific refactors/config/audits that do not apply, while overlooking the real framework. Expectation: a framework attribution reflects a framework the repo actually uses (or is gated on a dependency/manifest signal), not the pattern matcher's static guess. Related but distinct from WI-babun (the framework_dispatch vs profile.frameworks two-surface contradiction, fastapi=18 absent from profile) and WI-napuj (root: frameworks have no node-level provenance, the E03 enrichment target) — this row is the producer-level dep-blind _PATTERN_TYPE_TO_FRAMEWORK fix on the server_framework meta key, which can close independently. Also sibling of WI-zurig (U19: WS fixtures in test files) and WI-mulub (server_framework unregistered in MetaKeySpec). Cross-ref WI-babun, WI-napuj, WI-zurig, WI-mulub."  # 43d4
